Not about the neglected significant other, and not about FTP, but the 
rest is on the money - the problem lies somewhere on your side.

I had a look at the Hearse logs and I can see your web requests to 
upload, but no requests to download.  In other words, your download 
request never even made it near the Hearse server and therefore the 
problem is on your computer or on your ISP.

502, as far as I can tell, means "Bad Gateway" or "Bad Proxy".  Are you 
using any weird and wonderful multiproxy-type programs?  Any antivirus 
software that might be jumping in and checking that the data going over 
the wire is clean?

Hearse relies on WinInet to do its dirty work.  Have you done anything 
evil and unpleasant to IE recently?  (e.g. partially upgraded and then 
aborted or something like that?)

